<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Death</h1>
<p>When you die you lose some of your experience points, unless you are level 3 or below. You lose half the experience you have above what your current level needed, but never more than half of what the next level takes and never less than a fifth of it. So it is a good idea to level as soon as you can.
</p><p>After you die a Valkyrie carries your soul away: to Valhalla if you are good, to the pits of Hel if you are evil, and into the astral planes if you are neutral. After a while (about a minute up to level 5, two minutes up to level 24, three from level 25) you are set down in the temple of Udgaard, or in your clan's home town if your clan has one.
</p><p>While you wait there, someone carrying your corpse, or standing by it, can cast resurrection or raise dead on you. You still lose the experience points, but it shortens your stay: you come back to life where the caster stands, with everything that was in your corpse.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Your_corpse">Your corpse</span></h2>
<p>Your corpse stays where you died, with everything you carried, your coins too. Go back and get your things: get all from corpse (see <a cmd='#'>Help Get</a>).
</p><p>If it isn't there, it may have been moved. Look in the Village Crypt, down from the temple of Udgaard, where corpses can turn up. Giant worker ants roam the lands and carry corpses home to their mound in the hills, and going in after one is dangerous.
</p><p>Up to level 15 your soul is anchored to your body: a while after you die, your corpse and everything in it come back to the Village Crypt by themselves, wherever it was. From level 16 you need a Soul Anchor for that, and there is a shaman among the gremlins who knows how. An anchored corpse takes longer to come back the higher the level you died at: two minutes at level 1, about four at level 25, nine at level 50, eighteen at level 75 and half an hour from level 100. Without an anchor your corpse stays where it fell.
</p><p>If you want to see how many times you have died since January 1, 2006 type score. If you have died it will give you the amount of times. If you started playing after January 1 2006 then it will show the amount of deaths since you started.
</p><p><br />
